    "Question #: 7": {
      "Title": "Exam 500-443 topic 2 question 18 discussion - ExamTopics",
      "Question": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Which Routing Script logic helps to invoke the Post Call Survey successfully?"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Choices": {
        "A": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A. If the script completes after going to an Agent, the call is directed to the Post Call Survey dialed number."
            }
          ]
        },
        "B": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "B. To offer the PCS for all incoming DNs, there is no need to explicitly set the variable in the Main script. It is set to n by default."
            }
          ]
        },
        "C": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "C. If the script completes without going to an Agent, the call is directed to the Post Call Survey dialed number."
            }
          ]
        },
        "D": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "D. To offer the PCS for specific incoming DN\u2019s, the variable needs to be set in the Main script explicitly as n."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "Answer": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Suggested Answer: C \ud83d\uddf3\ufe0f"
          }
